Subject: [PATCH] Remove the retired API30 cross-user application exemption

One UI 9 forbids forks into mlsvendorcompat. Keep the current platform
assertion and the attribute declaration, but do not populate the obsolete
exception. Applications keep their ordinary per-user data policy.

diff --git a/mapping/30.0.compat.cil b/mapping/30.0.compat.cil
--- a/mapping/30.0.compat.cil
+++ b/mapping/30.0.compat.cil
@@ -9,3 +9,4 @@
 ;; mlsvendorcompat can be completely from the system policy.
-(typeattributeset mlsvendorcompat (and appdomain vendordomain))
+; One UI 9 no longer permits this cross-user application-data exemption.
+; Keep the attribute declared by the platform empty; its neverallow remains active.
 (allow mlsvendorcompat app_data_file (dir (ioctl read write create getattr setattr lock rename open watch watch_reads add_name remove_name reparent search rmdir)))
